  "seoTitle": "Basarnas and Regional Authorities Prepare for Rainy Season",
  "metaDescription": "Basarnas and regional officials across Indonesia are increasing personnel and disaster preparedness in anticipation of hydrometeorological threats.",
  "aiSummaryBullets": [
    "Basarnas has deployed personnel and held readiness assemblies in multiple regions including Riau Islands, Semarang, and Kendari.",
    "National and regional agencies are implementing strategies to mitigate risks related to the rainy season, such as floods and landslides.",
    "The Ministry of Social Affairs has mobilized 21,000 Tagana volunteers to assist with potential disaster responses nationwide."
  ],
  "aiContextParagraph": "Authorities across Indonesia are scaling up disaster preparedness measures as the country enters the rainy season. The National Search and Rescue Agency (Basarnas) has initiated readiness drills and increased staffing in several regions, including the Riau Islands, Semarang, and Kendari, to address potential hydrometeorological disasters. Simultaneously, the Ministry of Social Affairs has mobilized 21,000 personnel from the Disaster Preparedness Cadet (Tagana) program to ensure rapid response capabilities. Local governments and provincial police departments, such as those in West Java, are also coordinating efforts, including river normalization projects and the staging of thousands of personnel to handle emergencies like floods and landslides. These initiatives are supported by legislative bodies and national figures, who have emphasized the necessity of community and agency readiness to minimize the impact of adverse weather events across various provinces.",
